 html←prefix PrefixReadmeIds html
⍝ Puts `prefix` in front of every id in `html` and in front of every link pointing at one,
⍝ so that headings coming from somebody else's README cannot collide with the ids the page
⍝ generates for itself. Two elements sharing an id make invalid HTML, and the browser then
⍝ jumps to whichever came first - which would be ours, not theirs.
⍝ Links anywhere else are left alone: only an href that is nothing but a fragment can be
⍝ pointing at an id in this very page.
 html←('id="[^"]*"' 'href="[^"]*"')⎕R PrefixReadmeIds_⍠('IC' 1)⊣html
⍝Done
